!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Mouse embryonic stem cell line E14TG2a was cultured in DMEM Glutamax supplemented with 15% FBS, 1,000 U/mL of LIF, 0.1 mM of non-essential amino acids, 50 U/mL of penicillin and streptomycin and 0.1 mM of 2-mercaptoethanol.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = DNA samples were extracted using the NucleoSpin RNA purification kit and NucleoSpin RNA/DNA Buffer Set for parallel RNA and DNA purification (Macherey-Nagel) according to the manufacturer's instructions.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = RRBS libraries were prepared as described in Bender et al. (2021), Methods Mol Biol 2214:207-220. Briefly, 100 ng genomic DNA were digested with MspI (Thermo Fisher Scientific), end-repaired and A-tailed with Klenow fragment exo- (Thermo Fisher Scientific) and ligated to methylated adapters with T4 DNA ligase (Thermo Fisher Scientific) in Tango 1X buffer. DNA fragments ranging from 150 to 400 bp were selected by gel excision, purified using the MinElute gel extraction kit (Qiagen) and bisulfite-converted twice with the EpiTect bisulfite kit (Qiagen). The libraries were amplified using the Pfu Turbo Cx hotstart DNA polymerase (Agilent) with 12 PCR cycles and purified using Agencourt AmpureXP beads (Beckman-Coulter).
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were trimmed with Trim Galore (v0.4.4) in –non_directional and –rrbs mode to remove adapter sequences, two bases filled in during end-repair of MspI restriction sites, and low-quality ends with a Phred score below 20. Sequencing reads were mapped to the mouse genome (mm10) with Bismark v0.18.2 with default parameters. Methylation scores were extracted as the ratio of the number of Cs over the total number of Cs and Ts using the Bismark_methylation_extractor. CpG methylation ratios from both strands were combined and filtered for a minimum sequencing depth of 8X.
!Sample_data_processing = We provide IGV files containing methylation scores for all CGs with at least 8X sequencing depth.
!Sample_platform_id = GPL21103
!Sample_contact_name = Michael,,Weber
!Sample_contact_department = UMR7242 Biotechnology and Cell Signalling
